# Resolved by `op run` when an approved episode is staged. Committed on
# purpose: every op:// below is a REFERENCE, not a value, and resolving one
# needs an unlocked 1Password account this file knows nothing about.
#
#   ./tools/episode.py stage ep1          # wraps itself in op run with this file
#   op run --env-file=tools/stage.env -- ./tools/stage.py ep1
#
# The token is the podcast one, not the tfstate one and not the backup one:
# Object Read & Write on these two buckets and nothing else (infra/podcast/r2.tf).
# Item type API Credential, so the fields are username + credential.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=9468eccb7caed9f96283a9139c37a4df
R2_ARCHIVE_BUCKET=agentsee-podcast-archive
R2_MEDIA_BUCKET=agentsee-media
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=op://Engineering/R2 podcast token/username
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=op://Engineering/R2 podcast token/credential
